The attached image displays the anti-rPA IgG titers in mice immunized with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) alone or formulated with various doses of aluminum hydroxide (AH) or Nano-11 adjuvant. It demonstrates that both AH and Nano-11 significantly enhance the antibody response to rPA compared to soluble rPA (*p < 0.01 vs. soluble rPA). Specifically, Nano-11 at 200 µg/dose and 50 µg/dose induces antibody titers comparable to or greater than those achieved with AH at similar concentrations, with the median anti-rPA IgG titers for Nano-11-adjuvanted groups reaching 10^5 or higher.